&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;As a Commercial Strategy &amp;amp; Program Manager in our Sales Strategy &amp;amp; Operations team, you’ll manage the commercial go-to-market for on-top products across our international markets. With a particular focus on new product launches, you’ll build the business case, define the commercial approach and lead cross-functional execution from launch preparation through adoption and scaling.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;You’ll be the central commercial point of contact for your assigned products, working closely with Product, Product Marketing, local sales leadership, Pricing, Finance and Analytics. You’ll turn analysis into decisions and strategy, align teams around measurable objectives and drive action when performance falls short.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;This role is ideal for someone with a consulting or commercial strategy background who wants to combine analytical depth with hands-on responsibility for product commercialization.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Own go-to-market plans:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Define target customers, sales motions, market sequencing and launch priorities for on-top products. Drive execution against clear milestones and responsibilities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Build and challenge business cases:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Quantify revenue potential, expected uptake and commercial costs. Test assumptions and make clear recommendations on launch and scaling opportunities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Shape the commercial proposition:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Work with Product Marketing, Pricing and local markets to translate dealer value into a compelling commercial offer, customer targeting and sales approach.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Drive cross-functional launch readiness:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Evaluate commercial preparation, recommend market rollout sequencing and present risks, trade-offs and recommendations to leadership&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Manage commercial performance:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Agree KPIs, targets and reporting requirements before launch. Analyze adoption, usage, sales conversion and revenue contribution to identify what drives or limits growth.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Turn performance insights into improvements:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Lead structured performance reviews and coordinate action plans with clear owners and timelines, escalating unresolved dependencies where needed.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Strengthen commercialization practices:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Develop reusable business case and performance-management frameworks, capture lessons learned and ensure a clear handover to ongoing owners.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;What you’ll bring:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;4+ years of experience in management consulting, commercial strategy, sales strategy and operations, or a similarly analytical business role.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Experience building business cases, financial models and performance analyses, with the ability to test assumptions and explain their business implications.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;A track record of leading cross-functional initiatives from recommendation through implementation, ideally involving product launches or commercial growth.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Sound commercial judgment and an understanding of how customer value, pricing and sales execution translate into adoption and revenue.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The ability to structure complex problems, present clear recommendations and influence senior stakeholders without direct reporting authority.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;A pragmatic, collaborative approach, with the drive to resolve obstacles and follow through on results.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Excellent communication skills in English; German is a big plus.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;Scopely is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Product Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to join our &lt;strong&gt;Star Trek™ Fleet Command&lt;/strong&gt; team in London on a hybrid basis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Star Trek Fleet Command&#39;s ongoing success goes from strength to strength. Our in-house developed 4X MMO was launched in 2018 and continues to evolve, being consistently one of the top grossing Massive Multiplayer Strategy games on the market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Scopely, we care deeply about what we do and want to inspire play, every day - whether in our work environments alongside our talented colleagues or through our deep connections with our communities of players. We are a global team of game lovers who are developing, publishing, and innovating the mobile games industry, connecting millions of people around the world daily.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Senior Product Manager&lt;strong&gt;, &lt;/strong&gt;you will be the product owner for key monetisation and engagement initiatives across the live game. This includes driving the roadmap and execution of our monthly content releases, ensuring they are cohesive, compelling, and highly performant. You will work cross-functionally with Game Design, Product Marketing, Product Ops, Economy Design, and Data Science teams to define, prioritise, and deliver exceptional player experiences that meet business and player goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the content and performance strategy for our monthly releases, aligning them to player motivations, economic balance, and business KPIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and manage the monthly content calendar, collaborating with Design, Production, and Engineering to deliver high-quality, on-time experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data and experimentation to optimise monetisation, engagement, and retention across a broad player lifecycle—from new users to end-game whales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deeply understand player behaviour across multiple geos and platforms to ensure we deliver value through personalisation and segmentation strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the economy and systems design teams to ensure content aligns with long-term progression goals and avoids inflation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with UX, Research, and Community teams to develop empathy for player sentiment and pain points, and translate them into actionable product improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build business cases for major new initiatives and content verticals, including competitive research and revenue forecasting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor junior PMs and contribute to a culture of product excellence and cross-functional collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience in product management, ideally with significant responsibility on a F2P mobile game&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success managing complex monetisation and engagement systems, with extensive experience in content development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-native mindset, with the ability to translate raw performance metrics into strategic insights and actionable plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and collaboration skills, with a proven track record of aligning diverse teams around a shared product vision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong player empathy and experience working with user research, community feedback, or other voice-of-player channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving impact across cross-functional pods, including creative, design, and engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Scopely, we create games for everyone - and want to ensure that the people behind our games reflect that!&amp;nbsp; We are committed to creating a diverse, supportive work environment where everyone is treated with respect. We are committed to providing equal employment opportunities and welcome individuals from all backgrounds to join us &amp;amp; embrace the adventure!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Scopely&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely is a leading video game and global interactive entertainment company, home to many of the world’s most beloved and enduring experiences, including two of the most successful mobile games of all-time “MONOPOLY GO!” and “Pokémon GO,” along with “Stumble Guys,” “Star Trek™ Fleet Command,” “MARVEL Strike Force,” “WWE Champions,” the Scrabble® franchise, “Yahtzee® With Buddies,” and many others. Across mobile, web, PC, and console, Scopely creates, develops, publishes, and live-operates one of the most diversified and award-winning portfolios in the games industry — bringing hundreds of millions of players together through a shared love of play.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2011, Scopely is powered by its exceptional team — including thousands of world-class gamemakers around the globe, a distinctive tenet-driven culture, and its proprietary technology platform, Playgami. Together, these strengths have fueled Scopely’s position as the #1 mobile games company in the U.S. and #2 globally, generating more than $10 billion in lifetime revenue. Whether building global sensations like “MONOPOLY GO!” from the ground up, or expanding through strategic acquisitions, including the FoxNext, GSN, and Scopely Explore games businesses — Scopely consistently delivers experiences players love today and return to for years to come.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recognized multiple times as one of the &quot;100 Most Influential Companies in the World&quot; by TIME magazine and one of Fast Company&#39;s &quot;World&#39;s Most Innovative Companies&quot; and “Best Workplaces for Innovators,” Scopely believes that video games can be a force for good — creating meaningful connections, vibrant communities, and making life better through play.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely has global operations and partners across four continents in more than a dozen countries worldwide. For more information, visit: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/&quot;&gt;https://www.scopely.com/&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notice to Candidates: Scopely will never request payment or financial information during the application or hiring process. Please apply only through our official &lt;a href=&quot;http://scopely.com&quot;&gt;website&lt;/a&gt; and verify that all Talent Partner communications come from an email address ending in @&lt;a href=&quot;http://scopely.com&quot;&gt;scopely.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Should you have any questions or encounter any fraudulent requests/emails/websites, please immediately contact ----- Our job applicant privacy policies are available here: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/en/job-applicant-privacy-notice-for-ca-residents&quot;&gt;California Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/en/eea-and-uk-job-applicant-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;EEA/UK Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employment at Scopely is based solely on a person&#39;s merit and qualifications. Scopely does not discriminate against any employee or applicant because of race, creed, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition (including breastfeeding), or any other basis protected by law. We also consider qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;img style=&quot;max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://assets.wp.lanes-planes.com/app/uploads/2025/12/Posting-header-banner.png&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;100%&quot;&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;styles-module__fieldItemName___s-uMO&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deine Position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;styles-module__fieldItemName___s-uMO&quot;&gt;Bei Lanes &amp;amp; Planes ist kein Tag wie der andere. Dein Fokus: Als Senior Product Manager verantwortest du mehrere große Produktthemen pro Quartal, von der Discovery bis zum messbaren Impact. Du verstehst Probleme erst tiefgehend, bevor du Lösungen baust, und zwar zunehmend selbst mit AI-Agenten, abgestimmt mit unseren Tech Leads. Du hältst Stakeholder aligned, steuerst komplexe Rollouts und belegst deinen Erfolg in Zahlen. Wenig Meetings, viel Fokuszeit.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;styles-module__fieldItemName___s-uMO&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;styles-module__fieldItemName___s-uMO&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dein Arbeitsalltag&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;styles-module__fieldItemName___s-uMO&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du verantwortest mehrere größere Produktthemen pro Quartal, von der Discovery über die Delivery bis zu Adoption und messbarem Impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du verstehst die Probleme unserer Kunden tiefgehend, gemeinsam mit Customer Success und Data, bevor du Lösungen baust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du entwickelst Lösungen zunehmend selbst mit AI-Agenten, vom Prototyp bis zu produktionsnahem Code, und stimmst Architektur, Qualität und Priorisierung mit unseren Tech Leads ab.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du triffst Entscheidungen in deinem Bereich selbst und hältst Stakeholder aus Finance, Customer Service und Engineering aligned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du steuerst Rollouts kontrolliert, gerade bei Supplier-Integrationen wie Hotelaggregatoren, und misst den Erfolg nach dem Launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du gestaltest den Wandel zu AI-first Development und unsere Priorisierung über Shape Up (Pitches, Betting Table) aktiv mit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wir arbeiten schriftlich und asynchron: wenig Meetings, viel Zeit für Discovery und Fokusarbeit.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;styles-module__fieldItemName___s-uMO&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dein Profil&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;styles-module__fieldItemName___s-uMO&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mindestens fünf Jahre Erfahrung im Product Management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Erfahrung mit komplexen, prozesslastigen B2B-Produkten, idealerweise in Fintech, Travel, Logistik oder SaaS mit Billing und Invoicing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nachweisbare End-to-End-Ownership: Discovery, Business Case, Implementation, Launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du triffst datengetriebene Entscheidungen und belegst sie mit Zahlen.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du arbeitest Lean und hypothesengetrieben.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du nutzt AI-Tools heute schon aktiv, für Prototyping, Analyse oder Code, und willst damit Produkte bauen, nicht nur Specs schreiben.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technisches Verständnis für APIs und Datenmodelle; du kannst von AI erzeugten Code einordnen und prüfen.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unternehmerischer Drive, hohe Eigenständigkeit, fließend Deutsch und Englisch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
